IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), THE SCHEDULE -- OFFENCES (src:3380-3541).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. The Schedule lists the offences for the purposes of subsections 21.31(2), (3) and (6)
-- (the access of investigative bodies to the register of individuals with significant control: piece cb1). The
-- Schedule is data. Items 1 to 8 are tables of provisions of eight Acts, GENERATED FROM THE TEXT BY A SCRIPT
-- (nothing is typed by hand, so no row can be mistyped); item 9 is a rule.
--
-- HOW THE TABLES ARE READ.
--   * One row is one provision: an Act, a section, a subsection. "Subsections 83.03(1) and (2)" is two rows.
--     A "section" with no subsection is one row marked as the whole section, which matches every subsection.
--   * The Customs Act (item 3) lists a provision only "in respect of the contravention of" named sections: one
--     row for each such section, and the section contravened is an input of the rule.
--   * A row carries the Schedule's own paragraph and the Schedule's own words for the offence.

§ `The Schedule -- offences`

§§ `The Acts the Schedule lists offences under`

-- src:3380 | SCHEDULE (Subsections 21.31(2), (3) and (6)) Offences
@ref CBCA Schedule heading (src:3380)
DECLARE `Act the Schedule lists offences under` IS ONE OF
    `the Criminal Code (Schedule item 1)`
    `the Copyright Act (Schedule item 2)`
    `the Customs Act (Schedule item 3)`
    `the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act (Schedule item 4)`
    `the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act (Schedule item 5)`
    `the Canadian Environmental Protection Act, 1999 (Schedule item 6)`
    `the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act (Schedule item 7)`
    `the Cannabis Act (Schedule item 8)`
    `any other Act (Schedule item 9)`

-- One provision of the Schedule: where it is, and what the Schedule calls it.
-- src:3380 | SCHEDULE (Subsections 21.31(2), (3) and (6)) Offences
@ref CBCA Schedule heading (src:3380)
DECLARE `Listed offence provision` HAS
    `the Act` IS A `Act the Schedule lists offences under`
    `the section` IS A STRING
    `the subsection` IS A STRING
    `the whole section is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only where the section contravened is` IS A STRING
    `paragraph of the Schedule` IS A STRING
    `what the Schedule calls it` IS A STRING

-- The one place the seven fields are put in order: every row below calls this and nothing else.
-- src:3380 | SCHEDULE (Subsections 21.31(2), (3) and (6)) Offences
@ref CBCA Schedule heading (src:3380)
GIVEN `the Act of the row` IS A `Act the Schedule lists offences under`
      `the section of the row` IS A STRING
      `the subsection of the row` IS A STRING
      `the whole section of the row is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section contravened that the row is limited to` IS A STRING
      `the paragraph of the Schedule` IS A STRING
      `the words the Schedule uses` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Listed offence provision`
DECIDE `a listed offence provision` IS
    `Listed offence provision` WITH
        `the Act` IS `the Act of the row`
        `the section` IS `the section of the row`
        `the subsection` IS `the subsection of the row`
        `the whole section is listed` IS `the whole section of the row is listed`
        `only where the section contravened is` IS `the section contravened that the row is limited to`
        `paragraph of the Schedule` IS `the paragraph of the Schedule`
        `what the Schedule calls it` IS `the words the Schedule uses`

