@ref CBCA Schedule (src:3381-3541)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Listed offence provision`
`the offence provisions listed in items 1 to 8 of the Schedule` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the offence provisions listed in item 1 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 2 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 3 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 4 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 5 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 6 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 7 of the Schedule`
      , `the offence provisions listed in item 8 of the Schedule`
    )

-- Items 1 to 8: a row matches when the Act and section are the offence's, the subsection is the offence's (or
-- the whole section is listed), and, for a row limited to a section contravened, that section is the one
-- contravened (pass "" when the offence is not under the Customs Act).
